# Force LF in the repository regardless of a given contributor's local
# core.autocrlf setting — Prettier's default endOfLine is "lf". This repo
# has been developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which converts
# LF to CRLF on checkout; without this file, any tool or editor that
# writes LF directly (this session's edits included) mixes CRLF and LF
# within the same file, which trips `prettier --check` on Linux CI
# regardless of whether the actual code content is fine. Added
# proactively alongside the CI format-check fix (see that commit — the
# specific failures found there were genuine pre-existing style
# violations like an over-long line, not confirmed to be line-ending
# issues themselves, but this closes the adjacent risk either way.
* text=auto eol=lf
